      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The main thing that the API brings to the table is closely watching the friends list so you have a good idea of WHEN someone unfriends you. \n\nUsers are still able to scroll through their friends list to see if someone is currently a friend...\n\nI have a friend request policy in that I ignore any friend requests that are sent to me without even speaking. One day I might add it to my BIO, one day..",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-22T00:12:41.633Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Unpopular opinion: enabling players to be notified about who unfriends them as it happens enables antisocial behavior, is harmful to mental health and results in things like “friend request policies” and weird parasocial dynamics which would never have happened in the first place if this information wasn’t queryable. It also doesn’t create anything of value.\n\nConsider closing this information to external sources outside of VRChat’s purview?",
